    "title": "pandas.Categorical.dtype — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Categorical.dtype#\n\n- property Categorical.dtype[source]#\n- The `CategoricalDtype` for this instance.See also \n  - `astype`\n  - Cast argument to a specified dtype.\n  - `CategoricalDtype`\n  - Type for categorical data.\n Examples >>> cat = pd.Categorical([\"a\", \"b\"], ordered=True) >>> cat ['a', 'b'] Categories (2, str): ['a' < 'b'] >>> cat.dtype CategoricalDtype(categories=['a', 'b'], ordered=True, categories_dtype=str)",
